{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SEhQTdAgF7DAYcnX9tw777","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge in observable behavior. This project stress-tests an AI code generation system (mage-claude-orchestrator) by deriving formal specs from C source, generating Go implementations, and verifying them via differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline per utility: extract (C source) → specify (human-authored PRD + use case) → synthesize (orchestrator-driven Go code generation) → verify (differential testing). Three shared libraries support all utilities: `pkg/testutils` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format` (output formatting). `magefiles/` provides build targets. Each utility lives in `cmd/<utility>/`.\n\n**Current state:** All specifications are written for releases 00.0 through 01.3. No generated code exists on the working branch -- previous generation output lives at `generation-merged` tags. All four release 00.0 use cases (magefiles, format, sys, testutils) show `codestatus: not started`.\n\n**Current release:** Release 00.0 (\"Batch 0 -- foundational infrastructure\") with four use cases remaining: uc001-magefiles, uc002-format, uc003-sys, uc004-testutils.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 contains four independent library packages plus build infrastructure. Dependency ordering (P5) dictates: foundational infrastructure before feature libraries, libraries before consumers. `pkg/testutils` is the most foundational component -- it implements the differential testing harness (ARCHITECTURE.yaml Design Decision 2: \"the primary verification mechanism\"). Without it, no utility implementation can be verified. `pkg/sys` and `pkg/format` are feature libraries needed by specific utilities; `magefiles` consumes all three. Starting with testutils unblocks all downstream verification.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/testutils: DiffTest struct and differential test runner -- rel00.0-uc004-testutils\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils component section and Design Decision 2)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find and read the testutils PRD in this directory)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (testutils test suite section)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct definition and differential test runner function\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Define the DiffTest struct with fields for command-line arguments, stdin input, environment variables, expected exit code, and optional expected stdout/stderr content, as specified in the testutils PRD\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement a runner function that executes both the Go binary under test and the GNU reference binary with identical stdin, arguments, and environment, then captures stdout, stderr, and exit code from each\n      - id: R3\n        text: Compare stdout, stderr, and exit code between the two binaries byte-for-byte by default, reporting divergences with the input that triggered them, the expected output (reference binary), and the actual output (Go binary)\n      - id: R4\n        text: Support configurable normalization hooks that transform output before comparison to handle known acceptable differences such as timestamps or path prefixes\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary file is difftest.go, named after the primary exported type DiffTest (project convention: name source files after the primary exported type, not the package name)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: Byte-for-byte comparison is the default mode per ARCHITECTURE.yaml Design Decision 2; normalization hooks are opt-in per test case\n      - id: D3\n        text: Both binaries receive identical stdin, arguments, and environment variables as specified in the ARCHITECTURE.yaml pkg/testutils capabilities\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: pkg/testutils/difftest.go exists and declares package testutils\n      - id: AC2\n        text: DiffTest struct is exported and contains all fields necessary to define a differential test case\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Runner function is exported and executes two binaries with matching inputs, returning structured comparison results\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Normalization hooks can be configured per DiffTest instance and are applied before comparison\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/ succeeds with no errors\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18057,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18057},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f9a3ab1-58a1-412d-abe5-edc4fc960d6b","uuid":"b6e69e1e-c59d-49dc-9ee7-85ae8394fd77"}
